        <p>Some may have helped a little. Some may not have helped at all.</p>
        <p>A calming treat is often given when stress is already visible. A pressure vest is usually saved for predictable events. A diffuser stays in one room. And even familiar training cues can become harder to follow when your dog is already near their limit.</p>
        <p>Each approach addresses a particular moment, place, or behavior.</p>
